Third-party material (the font, the music and the NFO art are NOT covered by the
MIT license above):

* assets/cp437_8x16.bin and tools/Px437_IBM_VGA_8x16.ttf are derived from
  "Px437 IBM VGA 8x16" from The Ultimate Oldschool PC Font Pack by VileR
  (https://int10h.org/oldschool-pc-fonts/), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 -- see
  tools/Px437-FONT-LICENSE.txt.
* The ASCII art in assets/scroller.nfo (logo, frame, section headers, bottom
  logo) is by Yce*Remorse, made for ENFUSiA's 2003 NFO; it remains the work of
  its author. Only the text inside the frame was written for this intro.
* assets/music.s3m is Aryx by Karsten Koch (1995), the tune the original
  2002 intro played. It remains the work and property of its author and is
  included only so the intro can play it, as it did in 2002.
* rust/src/s3m.rs is released under the MIT license above, but its playback
  rules, mixer arithmetic and resampler tables are modelled closely on OpenMPT's
  soundlib (libopenmpt), so OpenMPT's BSD-3-Clause notice applies to it as well:

